    "status": "present",
    "value": "Reverse the return trip so it becomes a second top-left to bottom-right path. Move both walkers one step at a time; after step t each is on the anti-diagonal r + c = t, so the state is just (t, r1, r2). Both previous positions came from one of four combinations (each walker moved down or right). The value of a state is the best previous value plus the cherries on both cells, counted once if the walkers share a cell. Requiring r1 <= r2 halves the states without losing anything because the walkers are interchangeable. Thorn cells and unreachable states use a sentinel."
  },
